+++ b/tools/mt6762/hardware/connectivity-memory/README.rst
@@ -0,0 +1,125 @@
+Connectivity memory admission and reservation proposal
+=====================================================
+
+This freestanding C core validates an executing boot's LK/FDT memory ownership
+snapshot and proposes two ranges. It performs no allocation, memory mapping,
+RAM access, zeroing, cache maintenance, MMIO, SMC, power or DMA operation.
+Default-off admission requires ``cm_request.enabled == 1``. Success is NOT a
+hardware grant or a committed reservation. There is no kernel/loader integration.
+
+Evidence and supported format
+-----------------------------
+
+The supplied LK ``lib/mblock/mblock_v2.h`` describes a native ARM structure;
+capture40's ``/memory/mblock_info`` contains exactly that 22,552-byte layout.
+It is little endian, unlike FDT cells. Offsets are decoded bytewise, never by
+casting possibly unaligned captured data to a native C structure:
+
+* Free count at0; 128 slots at8, stride24: start64, size64, rank32, padding.
+* Magic99999999 at3080, version2 at3084, reserved count at3088.
+* 128 reserved slots at3096, stride152: start64, size64, mapping32,
+  NUL-terminated name[128], padding.
+
+Counts are bounded by128; ranks by the LK format's four-rank maximum (not by
+FDT bank count). Mapping must be0/1, but neither value grants access. Padding
+and unused slots are deliberately ignored: they are not semantic fields.
+Selected reserved names must be nonempty, terminated printable ASCII. One
+zero-sized free slot is legitimate in capture40; its address must still fall
+within/on the end of a bank. Nonempty ranges must be overflow-free, each lie
+inside a supplied bank, and be pairwise disjoint across both ownership sets.
+Their sum must exactly cover the nonoverlapping FDT banks. Banks and totals
+are parameterized; the core does not hardcode a6GiB result.
+
+The existing unmodified physical FDT parser validates the entire container
+first. The second pass requires one mblock_info property on a root memory or
+memory@ node. Arbitrarily named device_type=memory nodes remain unsupported
+for locating this property and fail closed. The two exact reserved child
+names, compatible strings, no-map markers, sizes4MiB/3MiB and16MiB alignment
+must match. Disabled targets, preassigned reg, reusable/default DMA ownership,
+missing or duplicate significant fields are rejected. Bounds come from each
+node's actual alloc-ranges/alloc-range, not a compiled address suggestion.
+Every other dynamic owner's whole allocation interval stays excluded, even
+when equal to a target's interval. Fixed memreserve/reg must be contained in
+one LK reserved entry; spanning several adjacent entries conservatively fails.
+
+The current cells ``0 40000000 0 80000000`` describe [40000000,c0000000).
+The last pair is a SIZE, not an end address. Capture40 has18 free slots and28
+reserved entries, accounting for all6GiB. Its other dynamic owners conservatively
+exclude [40000000,a0000000) and [c0000000,d0000000). The eligible LK free extent
+[a0000000,b3330000) yields CONSYS[a0000000,a0400000) and Wi-Fi[a1000000,a1300000).
+These addresses are test results, never defaults. Captured raw FDT/table bytes
+remain private and are not part of this source package.
+
+Integration contract
+--------------------
+
+``cm_parse_mblock`` independently validates the table against caller-supplied,
+already validated banks. ``cm_plan`` takes the current immutable FDT and a
+caller-owned workspace (7,080 bytes on the64-bit host ABI; do not place it on a small kernel
+stack), an output ledger, and required live source-image, managed-kernel and
+loader/stack/scratch ranges. Each required range must be nonempty and contained
+in one actual bank. Include all other live allocations in ``additional``;
+unknown ownership is not inferred free. Overlapping exclusions are permitted.
+FDT physical address/length and reported framebuffer are excluded automatically.
+Inputs, workspace and output must not alias, and no concurrent writer may
+change the FDT during either validation pass.
+
+The search examines at most256*256 aligned pairs below4GiB, using backtracking
+so an early CONSYS choice cannot consume Wi-Fi's only valid location. Both
+ranges must independently fit inside one target interval and one LK-free
+entry. All real LK reservations are excluded by that disjoint ownership test.
+Errors zero the output ledger. A successful proposal records version, owner
+order, exact ranges, table counts/totals, FDT location and caller's fresh boot
+identifier. The identifier is provenance, not cryptographic authentication;
+a saved capture plus a made-up identifier cannot authorize physical use.
+
+Future integration must run this against the executing boot's live FDT,
+atomically commit both ranges to a single owned reservation ledger before any
+consumer can allocate/use them, bind that ledger to the same-image handoff,
+and preserve it for the full peripheral lifetime. It must not allocate from
+an earlier proposal after allocations change: pass the changed reservations
+and rerun. A repeat call with identical input is a repeat proposal, not an
+idempotent allocator. No old-boot ownership survives implicitly. Hashes in the
+host evidence establish artifact identity only, not freshness or quiescence.
+Any future expansion of general XNU RAM must consume the committed ledger.
+The current general FDT parser's conservative allocation exclusions remain
+unchanged, keeping both proposed ranges outside its managed window.
+
+Unmanaged mapping and remaining gates
+------------------------------------
+
+The selected ranges are below the current managed [d0000000,1bfe00000) window.
+They have no VM-page allocation ownership. XNU's io_map/pmap_map can map
+unmanaged physical ranges, but integration must carry explicit PA and VA;
+do not use phystokv/ml_static_ptovirt or kvtophys_nofail for these buffers.
+Do not broaden the platform's register-mapping allowlist to cover arbitrary RAM.
+A separate exact-range reservation capability is required. ml_io_map selects
+Device memory; ml_io_map_wcomb selects normal noncacheable memory. The correct
+cache/shareability policy for each firmware/descriptor/data use must be
+established separately, with no conflicting cached aliases and no assumption
+that peripheral DMA is coherent. The precompiled userspace16KiB VM and existing
+4KiB hardware PTE arrangement are untouched.
+
+CONN reset/power state, bus-master quiescence, EMI/secure-region permission,
+firmware identity/download, physical remap registers, and firmware's view of
+addresses are all independent outstanding prerequisites. The CONN remap's
+16MiB granularity explains the allocation alignment; it does not authorize
+programming it. No SMC or secure EMI operation is implemented. Capture40's
+free table is evidence of LK allocation ownership, not proof that an unknown
+firmware bus master cannot access the range. Reset/DA retention is unproved.
+
+Validation
+----------
+
+Run from any working directory::
+
+  python3 /path/to/connectivity-memory/test_conn_memory.py -v
+
+This compiles the actual core and unchanged FDT parser with C11, optimization,
+-Wall -Wextra -Werror and -ffreestanding. The optional private real-artifact
+check is enabled by ``CM_CAPTURE40=/path/to/capture40/runtime.dtb`` and requires
+its exact recorded SHA256. Synthetic tests remain self-contained and cover
+malformed/truncated tables/FDT, overflow, count/rank/name/mapping errors,
+coverage/overlap, changed and duplicate owners, fixed ownership inconsistency,
+other dynamic exclusions, live exclusions, no-space and pair backtracking.
+The tests make no device accesses and write no actual physical RAM.
diff --git a/tools/mt6762/hardware/connectivity-memory/conn_memory.c b/tools/mt6762/hardware/connectivity-memory/conn_memory.c
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..d16c0362a4eee6533922bf0d8e648fc1326d9f2c
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tools/mt6762/hardware/connectivity-memory/conn_memory.c
@@ -0,0 +1,227 @@
+#include "conn_memory.h"
+
+static void zero(void *p, size_t n) { unsigned char *b=p; while (n--) *b++=0; }
+static uint32_t le32(const unsigned char *p) {
+    return (uint32_t)p[0]|(uint32_t)p[1]<<8|(uint32_t)p[2]<<16|(uint32_t)p[3]<<24;
+}
+static uint64_t le64(const unsigned char *p) { return le32(p)|((uint64_t)le32(p+4)<<32); }
+static uint32_t be32(const unsigned char *p) {
+    return (uint32_t)p[3]|(uint32_t)p[2]<<8|(uint32_t)p[1]<<16|(uint32_t)p[0]<<24;
+}
+static uint64_t be64(const unsigned char *p) { return (uint64_t)be32(p)<<32|be32(p+4); }
+static int equal(const char *a, const char *b) {
+    while (*a && *a==*b) { a++; b++; } return *a==*b;
+}
+static int prefix(const char *a, const char *b) {
+    while (*b) if (*a++!=*b++) return 0;
+    return 1;
+}
+static int valid(struct mtk_fdt_range a) { return a.size && a.base<=UINT64_MAX-a.size; }
+static int inside(struct mtk_fdt_range a, struct mtk_fdt_range b) {
+    return valid(a) && valid(b) && a.base>=b.base && a.base+a.size<=b.base+b.size;
+}
+static int overlap(struct mtk_fdt_range a, struct mtk_fdt_range b) {
+    return a.size && b.size && a.base<b.base+b.size && b.base<a.base+a.size;
+}
+static int covered(struct mtk_fdt_range a, const struct mtk_fdt_range *v, size_t n) {
+    size_t i; for (i=0;i<n;i++) if (inside(a,v[i])) return 1;
+    return 0;
+}
+static int parse_table(const unsigned char *b, size_t n,
+    const struct mtk_fdt_range *banks, size_t bank_count, struct cm_table *t) {
+    size_t i,j; uint32_t nf,nr;
+    if (!b || !banks || !bank_count || bank_count>MTK_FDT_MAX_MEMORY) return CM_ARGUMENT;
+    if (n!=CM_MBLOCK_BYTES || le32(b+3080)!=0x99999999 || le32(b+3084)!=2) return CM_FORMAT;
+    nf=le32(b); nr=le32(b+3088);
+    if (nf>CM_MAX_BLOCKS || nr>CM_MAX_BLOCKS) return CM_COUNT;
+    for (i=0;i<bank_count;i++) {
+        if (!valid(banks[i]) || t->bank_bytes>UINT64_MAX-banks[i].size) return CM_RANGE;
+        for (j=0;j<i;j++) if (overlap(banks[i],banks[j])) return CM_OVERLAP;
+        t->bank_bytes+=banks[i].size;
+    }
+    t->free_count=nf; t->reserved_count=nr;
+    for (i=0;i<(size_t)nf+nr;i++) {
+        int free_slot=i<nf; size_t k=free_slot?i:i-nf;
+        const unsigned char *p=free_slot?b+8+k*24:b+3096+k*152;
+        struct mtk_fdt_range a={le64(p),le64(p+8)};
+        if (free_slot) {
+            if (le32(p+16)>3) return CM_FORMAT; /* LK supports four DRAM ranks. */
+            if (!a.size) {
+                int in_bank=0;
+                for (j=0;j<bank_count;j++)
+                    if (a.base>=banks[j].base && a.base<=banks[j].base+banks[j].size) in_bank=1;
+                if (!in_bank) return CM_RANGE;
+                t->free[k]=a; continue;
+            }
+        } else {
+            if (le32(p+16)>1) return CM_FORMAT; /* mapping flag, not a grant. */
+            for (j=0;j<128 && p[20+j];j++)
+                if (p[20+j]<32 || p[20+j]>126) return CM_FORMAT;
+            if (!j || j==128) return CM_FORMAT;
+        }
+        if (!valid(a) || !covered(a,banks,bank_count)) return CM_RANGE;
+        if (free_slot) { t->free[k]=a; t->free_bytes+=a.size; }
+        else { t->reserved[k]=a; t->reserved_bytes+=a.size; }
+        /* Every nonempty range must be disjoint, including across owner sets.
+         * Therefore the running total cannot overflow the bank total. */
+        for (j=0;j<i;j++) {
+            struct mtk_fdt_range prev=j<nf?t->free[j]:t->reserved[j-nf];
+            if (overlap(a,prev)) return CM_OVERLAP;
+        }
+    }
+    if (t->free_bytes>t->bank_bytes || t->reserved_bytes!=t->bank_bytes-t->free_bytes)
+        return CM_COVERAGE;
+    return CM_OK;
+}
+int cm_parse_mblock(const void *bytes, size_t n, const struct mtk_fdt_range *banks,
+    size_t bank_count, struct cm_table *out) {
+    int e; if (!out) return CM_ARGUMENT;
+    zero(out,sizeof(*out)); e=parse_table(bytes,n,banks,bank_count,out);
+    if (e) zero(out,sizeof(*out));
+    return e;
+}
+
+struct node_data {
+    const unsigned char *alloc, *reg, *size, *align, *compat, *status;
+    uint32_t alloc_n, reg_n, size_n, align_n, compat_n, status_n;
+    unsigned int seen, no_map; int target;
+};
+static int string_value(const unsigned char *p, uint32_t n, const char *s) {
+    uint32_t i=0; if (!p) return 0;
+    while (s[i]) { if (i>=n || p[i]!=(unsigned char)s[i]) return 0; i++; }
+    return n==i+1 && p[i]==0;
+}
+static int finish_node(struct node_data *d, struct cm_workspace *w, unsigned *targets) {
+    uint32_t i,n; struct mtk_fdt_range *v; uint32_t *count;
+    if (d->target>=0) {
+        unsigned mask=1U<<(unsigned)d->target;
+        uint64_t expected=d->target?CM_WIFI_BYTES:CM_CONSYS_BYTES;
+        if (*targets&mask) return CM_OWNER;
+        *targets|=mask;
+        if (d->reg || !d->no_map || d->size_n!=8 || d->align_n!=8 ||
+            be64(d->size)!=expected || be64(d->align)!=CM_ALIGNMENT ||
+            !string_value(d->compat,d->compat_n,d->target?"shared-dma-pool":"mediatek,consys-reserve-memory") ||
+            (d->status && !string_value(d->status,d->status_n,"okay") &&
+             !string_value(d->status,d->status_n,"ok"))) return CM_OWNER;
+        if (!d->alloc || !d->alloc_n || d->alloc_n%16) return CM_OWNER;
+        v=w->allowed[d->target]; count=&w->allowed_count[d->target];
+        n=d->alloc_n/16; if (n>CM_MAX_CONSTRAINTS) return CM_COUNT;
+    } else {
+        if (d->reg || !d->alloc) return CM_OK;
+        v=w->other_dynamic; count=&w->other_count; n=d->alloc_n/16;
+        if (!d->alloc_n || d->alloc_n%16 || n>64-*count) return CM_COUNT;
+    }
+    for (i=0;i<n;i++) {
+        struct mtk_fdt_range a={be64(d->alloc+i*16),be64(d->alloc+i*16+8)};
+        if (!valid(a)) return CM_RANGE;
+        v[(*count)++]=a;
+    }
+    return CM_OK;
+}
+/* Called only after mtk_fdt_parse has validated every token, name and extent.
+ * This pass preserves reserved child identity rather than subtracting ranges
+ * by equality (an unrelated owner can have exactly the same alloc-ranges). */
+static int extract(const unsigned char *b, struct cm_workspace *w) {
+    uint32_t pos=be32(b+8), end=pos+be32(b+36), strings=be32(b+12);
+    unsigned depth=0, targets=0; int reserved_root=0, memory_node=0, found=0;
+    struct node_data d; zero(&d,sizeof(d)); d.target=-1;
+    while (pos<end) {
+        uint32_t token=be32(b+pos); pos+=4;
+        if (token==1) {
+            const char *name=(const char *)(b+pos); uint32_t len=0;
+            while (b[pos+len]) len++;
+            pos=(pos+len+4)&~3U; depth++;
+            if (depth==2) {
+                reserved_root=equal(name,"reserved-memory");
+                memory_node=equal(name,"memory") || prefix(name,"memory@");
+            }
+            if (depth==3 && reserved_root) {
+                zero(&d,sizeof(d)); d.target=-1;
+                if (equal(name,"consys-reserve-memory")) d.target=0;
+                if (equal(name,"wifi-reserve-memory")) d.target=1;
+            }
+        } else if (token==2) {
+            if (depth==3 && reserved_root) { int e=finish_node(&d,w,&targets); if (e) return e; }
+            if (depth==2) { reserved_root=0; memory_node=0; }
+            depth--;
+        } else if (token==3) {
+            uint32_t n=be32(b+pos), nameoff=be32(b+pos+4); const unsigned char *p=b+pos+8;
+            const char *name=(const char *)(b+strings+nameoff); unsigned bit=0;
+            pos=(pos+8+n+3)&~3U;
+            if (depth==2 && memory_node && equal(name,"mblock_info")) {
+                int e; if (found++) return CM_OWNER;
+                e=cm_parse_mblock(p,n,w->info.memory,w->info.memory_count,&w->table); if (e) return e;
+            }
+            if (depth!=3 || !reserved_root) continue;
+            if (equal(name,"reg")) { bit=1; d.reg=p; d.reg_n=n; }
+            else if (equal(name,"alloc-ranges") || equal(name,"alloc-range")) { bit=2; d.alloc=p; d.alloc_n=n; }
+            else if (equal(name,"size")) { bit=4; d.size=p; d.size_n=n; }
+            else if (equal(name,"alignment")) { bit=8; d.align=p; d.align_n=n; }
+            else if (equal(name,"compatible")) { bit=16; d.compat=p; d.compat_n=n; }
+            else if (equal(name,"status")) { bit=32; d.status=p; d.status_n=n; }
+            else if (equal(name,"no-map")) { bit=64; if (n) return CM_OWNER; d.no_map=1; }
+            else if (d.target>=0 && (equal(name,"reusable") || equal(name,"linux,cma-default") || equal(name,"linux,dma-default"))) return CM_OWNER;
+            if (bit&d.seen) return CM_OWNER;
+            d.seen|=bit;
+        } else if (token==9) break;
+    }
+    return found==1 && targets==3?CM_OK:CM_OWNER;
+}
+static int available(struct mtk_fdt_range a, unsigned target,
+    const struct cm_workspace *w, const struct cm_request *r, struct mtk_fdt_range selected) {
+    size_t i; struct mtk_fdt_range dt={r->fdt_pa,w->info.total_size};
+    if (!covered(a,w->table.free,w->table.free_count) ||
+        !covered(a,w->allowed[target],w->allowed_count[target]) || overlap(a,selected) ||
+        overlap(a,r->source_image) || overlap(a,r->kernel_managed) || overlap(a,r->loader_live) ||
+        overlap(a,dt)) return 0;
+    for (i=0;i<w->other_count;i++) if (overlap(a,w->other_dynamic[i])) return 0;
+    for (i=0;i<r->additional_count;i++) if (overlap(a,r->additional[i])) return 0;
+    if (w->info.framebuffer.present && w->info.framebuffer.size) {
+        struct mtk_fdt_range fb={w->info.framebuffer.base,w->info.framebuffer.size};
+        if (overlap(a,fb)) return 0;
+    }
+    return 1;
+}
+int cm_plan(const void *blob, size_t n, const struct cm_request *r,
+    struct cm_workspace *w, struct cm_ledger *out) {
+    size_t i; unsigned c,f; int e; struct mtk_fdt_range empty={0,0}, dt;
+    if (!out) return CM_ARGUMENT;
+    zero(out,sizeof(*out));
+    if (!r || !w || !blob) return CM_ARGUMENT;
+    if (r->enabled!=1) return CM_DISABLED;
+    if (r->reserved_zero || !r->boot_nonce || r->additional_count>CM_MAX_EXTRA ||
+        (r->additional_count && !r->additional) || !valid(r->source_image) ||
+        !valid(r->kernel_managed) || !valid(r->loader_live)) return CM_ARGUMENT;
+    for (i=0;i<r->additional_count;i++) if (!valid(r->additional[i])) return CM_RANGE;
+    zero(w,sizeof(*w));
+    if (mtk_fdt_parse(blob,n,&w->info) || !w->info.board_compatible) return CM_FDT;
+    dt.base=r->fdt_pa; dt.size=w->info.total_size;
+    if (!covered(dt,w->info.memory,w->info.memory_count) ||
+        !covered(r->source_image,w->info.memory,w->info.memory_count) ||
+        !covered(r->kernel_managed,w->info.memory,w->info.memory_count) ||
+        !covered(r->loader_live,w->info.memory,w->info.memory_count)) return CM_RANGE;
+    e=extract(blob,w); if (e) return e;
+    /* Every actual fixed reservation must have LK ownership evidence. A new
+     * fixed node overlapping advertised free space is an inconsistent handoff. */
+    for (i=0;i<w->info.reserved_count;i++)
+        if (w->info.reserved_kind[i]!=MTK_FDT_RESERVE_ALLOC &&
+            !covered(w->info.reserved[i],w->table.reserved,w->table.reserved_count)) return CM_OWNER;
+    /* Exhaustive bounded two-owner search below4GiB: at most256*256 pairs.
+     * Backtracking prevents a greedy CONSYS choice from starving Wi-Fi. */
+    for (c=0;c<256;c++) {
+        struct mtk_fdt_range a={(uint64_t)c*CM_ALIGNMENT,CM_CONSYS_BYTES};
+        if (!available(a,0,w,r,empty)) continue;
+        for (f=0;f<256;f++) {
+            struct mtk_fdt_range b={(uint64_t)f*CM_ALIGNMENT,CM_WIFI_BYTES};
+            if (!available(b,1,w,r,a)) continue;
+            out->version=1; out->count=2; out->boot_nonce=r->boot_nonce;
+            out->fdt_pa=r->fdt_pa; out->fdt_bytes=w->info.total_size;
+            out->proposed[0]=a; out->proposed[1]=b;
+            out->bank_bytes=w->table.bank_bytes; out->free_bytes=w->table.free_bytes;
+            out->lk_reserved_bytes=w->table.reserved_bytes;
+            out->lk_free_count=w->table.free_count; out->lk_reserved_count=w->table.reserved_count;
+            return CM_OK;
+        }
+    }
+    return CM_NO_SPACE;
+}
diff --git a/tools/mt6762/hardware/connectivity-memory/conn_memory.h b/tools/mt6762/hardware/connectivity-memory/conn_memory.h
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..95afb0a4de9f6d01c9a0b94935aea58e182c9c57
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tools/mt6762/hardware/connectivity-memory/conn_memory.h
@@ -0,0 +1,56 @@
+#ifndef MT6762_CONN_MEMORY_H
+#define MT6762_CONN_MEMORY_H
+#include <stdint.h>
+#include <stddef.h>
+#include "../../physical/fdt_handoff.h"
+#define CM_MBLOCK_BYTES 22552U
+#define CM_MAX_BLOCKS 128U
+#define CM_MAX_CONSTRAINTS 16U
+#define CM_MAX_EXTRA 64U
+#define CM_ALIGNMENT UINT64_C(0x1000000)
+#define CM_CONSYS_BYTES UINT64_C(0x400000)
+#define CM_WIFI_BYTES UINT64_C(0x300000)
+/* No error grants memory, mappings, DMA, power or peripheral ownership. */
+enum cm_error { CM_OK=0, CM_DISABLED=-1, CM_ARGUMENT=-2, CM_FDT=-3,
+    CM_FORMAT=-4, CM_COUNT=-5, CM_RANGE=-6, CM_OVERLAP=-7,
+    CM_COVERAGE=-8, CM_OWNER=-9, CM_NO_SPACE=-10 };
+struct cm_table {
+    struct mtk_fdt_range free[CM_MAX_BLOCKS], reserved[CM_MAX_BLOCKS];
+    uint32_t free_count, reserved_count;
+    uint64_t free_bytes, reserved_bytes, bank_bytes;
+};
+struct cm_request {
+    uint32_t enabled, reserved_zero;
+    /* Caller-supplied fresh boot identifier, NOT authentication/attestation. */
+    uint64_t boot_nonce, fdt_pa;
+    /* Required complete owned ranges. They may overlap each other. */
+    struct mtk_fdt_range source_image, kernel_managed, loader_live;
+    const struct mtk_fdt_range *additional;
+    size_t additional_count;
+};
+struct cm_ledger {
+    uint32_t version, count;
+    uint64_t boot_nonce, fdt_pa, fdt_bytes;
+    /* Entries in immutable order: CONSYS, Wi-Fi. Proposal only, not committed. */
+    struct mtk_fdt_range proposed[2];
+    uint64_t bank_bytes, free_bytes, lk_reserved_bytes;
+    uint32_t lk_free_count, lk_reserved_count;
+};
+/* Caller owns this workspace. No allocation and no large automatic arrays.
+ * Workspace, output, request, FDT and input ranges must not alias. */
+struct cm_workspace {
+    struct mtk_fdt_info info;
+    struct cm_table table;
+    struct mtk_fdt_range allowed[2][CM_MAX_CONSTRAINTS], other_dynamic[64];
+    uint32_t allowed_count[2], other_count;
+};
+/* Exact LE LK mblock v2 ABI; banks come from validated live FDT. Empty free
+ * slots are permitted; nonempty ranges must partition the supplied banks. */
+int cm_parse_mblock(const void *bytes, size_t size,
+    const struct mtk_fdt_range *banks, size_t bank_count, struct cm_table *out);
+/* Revalidate the executing boot's immutable FDT each call. Capture files are
+ * suitable ONLY for offline tests. A successful proposal has no side effects;
+ * caller must atomically commit the ledger before any mapping/consumer use. */
+int cm_plan(const void *fdt, size_t accessible, const struct cm_request *request,
+    struct cm_workspace *workspace, struct cm_ledger *out);
+#endif
