new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..b095f89842444ea940bfb501075d503214ea7145
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tools/mt6762/hardware/connectivity-power/README.rst
@@ -0,0 +1,135 @@
+Passive connectivity survey, record version 1
+============================================
+
+``../../physical/connectivity_probe.h`` collects two sequential observations
+of 21 AP and 19 PMIC ordinary words. This is a prerequisite observation for
+native connectivity power work; it does not power CONN, grant ownership, or
+show that firmware or an oscillator is running. The closed address list and
+source references are in ``registers.json``. No address in the CONN 0x180xxxxx
+domain, SET/CLR alias, ADC request, IRQ acknowledgment or oscillator AUXOUT
+selector is included.
+
+Integration contract
+--------------------
+
+The owner calls ``mt6762_connectivity_capture(io, record, identity, enabled)``
+only after reserving a writable, aligned 4096-byte record. Exactly ``enabled=1``
+executes hardware callbacks. Zero initializes a DISABLED record without calling
+any callback, including the barrier/timer. All other values fail. No default
+hardware call site or compile-time enable is supplied by this module. A loader
+integration must default its flag off and must not turn survey completion into
+an ADT ownership grant.
+
+The proposed retained range is [0x40085400, 0x40086400), immediately following
+the peripheral record. The module does not allocate or reserve this range.
+The linker, producer, reader and XNU memory exclusions must agree before use.
+The owner must retain/cache-clean the completed or failed record. State commits
+alone do not flush cache or independently establish physical retention.
+
+Provide bounded callbacks with zero indicating success, output untouched on
+failure, and an ordering barrier. The timer must be the proven 13 MHz counter.
+The default global budget is 250000 us, configurable from 1 through 1000000 us.
+The collector makes at most 80 read calls, without retries, and stops at the
+first transport error, clock rejection, PMIC family mismatch or elapsed budget.
+Times are unsigned 64-bit counter values; modular elapsed arithmetic tolerates
+wrap. Even a frozen timer cannot cause an infinite collector loop. Budget checks
+between calls cannot interrupt a stalled bus or a stuck callback. Synchronous
+abort, asynchronous SError and a peripheral hanging the interconnect are not
+contained by this code.
+
+``read_ap32`` must enforce the actual loader's mapped, AP-readable whitelist and
+live clock admission. The collector checks its earlier same-pass INFRA+0x90
+bit 1 before the PWRAP configuration window, but this snapshot does not replace
+the callback's live PWRAP gate check. It never follows mutable record addresses.
+No supply/reset/protection/pinmux/DMA write callback exists.
+
+``pwrap_readonly.h`` adapts the unchanged native
+``bsd/dev/mt6762_power_protocol.h`` LK22 WACS engine. Supply an exclusive bounded
+acquire/release pair, the actual register/delay callbacks, and live inherited
+LK22 wrapper admission under that ownership. The adapter's admission means
+wrapper admission, not an assumed PMIC identity. Every PMIC pass starts with
+ordinary HWCID 0x0008; the core requires bits 15:8 == 0x57 before any other PMIC
+word. A successful mismatched ID is retained as a valid raw sample, with record
+result -6 and no later PMIC access. The low revision byte is not constrained.
+
+WACS necessarily writes a READ command to WACS2_CMD and VLDCLR for that completed
+read. These are transport operations, not writes to PMIC registers. The adapter
+never sets command bit 31, never retries/reinitializes the wrapper, and latches
+any transaction/admission failure. Subsequent calls cannot clear another
+owner's pending response. Existing bounded WACS polling and errors are retained.
+The owner must not run competing PWRAP users or release ownership while a
+transaction is pending. Observation does not authorize later regulator writes.
+
+Frozen wire format
+------------------
+
+All fields are little-endian, with no implicit packed/pointer-dependent fields.
+
+* Header: 112 bytes, magic ``MTKCONN1``, version 1, size 4096, 32-byte payload
+  identity; state and complement, one-based pass (zero before start), last
+  attempted index (0xffffffff before start), two begin and two end counter
+  values, frequency/budget, result and original transport error.
+* Forty entries at offset 112, each 24 bytes: address u32, bus u8, width u8,
+  validity u16, two raw u32 values, two signed i32 errors. Bits 0/1 commit the
+  respective pass. Unattempted errors are INT32_MIN. AP indices are 0..20;
+  PMIC HWCID is index 21. A successful but late callback retains its valid value
+  while the overall record fails the deadline.
+* Offset 1072 through 4095: 3024 reserved zero bytes.
+
+States are NOT_STARTED=0, DISABLED=1, READING=2, COMPLETE=3, FAILED=4. Results are
+OK=0, OFF=1, ARGUMENT=-1, TRANSPORT=-2, DEADLINE=-3, TIMER=-4, PWRAP_GATED=-5,
+PMIC_FAMILY=-6. Per-entry errors describe callbacks or a pre-read rejection;
+the separate overall result describes post-read deadline/family rejection.
+
+``record.py initialize --identity HEX64 --output FILE`` emits a pristine
+NOT_STARTED packet. ``record.py decode FILE --expected-identity HEX64`` validates
+identity, ABI, fixed addresses/widths, state complement, validity, completion,
+reserved bytes and family rejection. COMPLETE timestamps must follow first
+start, first end, second start, second end, within the global budget; ordering
+uses unsigned offsets from first start to permit counter wrap. Equal times
+remain valid. NOT_STARTED/DISABLED require all raw sample slots to be zero.
+Treat a torn state commit as invalid and
+keep the raw file for investigation. Decoding is an offline operation; metadata
+must never be used as an MMIO execution list or an ownership grant.
+
+Evidence and interpretation
+---------------------------
+
+``provenance.json`` binds the private shipped-artifact audits by digest without
+redistributing their binaries. The shipped WMT driver uses CCF for CONN power;
+inactive BSP fallback loops do not establish the shipped power sequence. The
+stock CCF power/ack/protection functions and WMT reset, pinmux and remap reads
+justify the AP words. Two extra pin-control words, 0x10002c00/0x10002c10, are in
+the shipped binary but their electrical labels remain unresolved.
+
+The exact stock clkbuf descriptor table proves PWRAP 0x188 bit 1 selects CONN
+automation and 0x18c..0x198 contain its four address/data words. PMIC 0x0788,
+0x07b0 and 0x044a are mapped by stock DT; optional 0x07ac bit 12 is interpreted
+only from the supplied MT6357 BSP header and optional I1 branch. Neither BSP
+automation template is asserted to be the actual inherited phone template.
+PMIC enable, DA and selector values are digital state, not measured voltage or
+frequency. DA stable bit 14 is a BSP interpretation; the shipped regulator
+table independently supports DA enable bit 15.
+
+Retained capture40 showed SPM primary/secondary 0x434c, with CONN bit 1 clear,
+and INFRA+0x90/+0x94 zero in both observations. This describes that handoff only;
+it does not establish current state, all rails off, BTIF configured, or valid
+oscillator output. No physical execution of this new collector is claimed by
+its host tests.
+
+Validation
+----------
+
+Run ``sh test.sh``. It executes the real C collector and existing WACS protocol,
+not a duplicate Python model: default-off/no callbacks; malformed inputs;
+80 transport fault positions; first/second pass family rejection; gate changes;
+deadline before/after reads, counter wrap/freeze; fixed execution addresses even
+when retained addresses are altered; all 19 allowed PMIC read commands and
+forbidden aliases; all three bounded WACS timeout phases and fault latching.
+Python consumes actual complete, partial-failure, wrong-family, counter-wrap
+and disabled C packets. It rejects corrupted fields, all inactive nonzero
+sample slots, and backwards/overlapping pass timestamps on ordinary or wrapped
+counters. Finally a real AArch64 freestanding consumer is
+compiled with -Wall -Wextra -Werror and checked for missing runtime symbols.
+Set ``CLANG`` to choose the compiler; otherwise the existing project toolchain
+is used when clang is absent from PATH. This is not a loader or kernel build.
diff --git a/tools/mt6762/hardware/connectivity-power/conn_power.c b/tools/mt6762/hardware/connectivity-power/conn_power.c
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..ee0d5aae714f1a872d9c4824aa10078c8a3c20fc
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tools/mt6762/hardware/connectivity-power/conn_power.c
@@ -0,0 +1,239 @@
+/* SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT */
+#include "conn_power.h"
+#include <stddef.h>
+
+#define RGU UINT32_C(0x10007018)
+#define SPM UINT32_C(0x1000632c)
+#define ACK0 UINT32_C(0x10006180)
+#define ACK1 UINT32_C(0x10006184)
+#define PROT_EN UINT32_C(0x10001220)
+#define PROT_ACK UINT32_C(0x10001228)
+#define PROT1_EN UINT32_C(0x10001250)
+#define PROT1_ACK UINT32_C(0x10001258)
+#define PROT_CLR UINT32_C(0x100012a4)
+#define PROT1_CLR UINT32_C(0x100012ac)
+#define CHIP_ID UINT32_C(0x180b1010)
+#define EXPECTED_ID UINT32_C(0x10020300)
+#define RESET UINT32_C(0x1000)
+#define RESET_KEY UINT32_C(0x88000000)
+#define PROT_MASK UINT32_C(0x16000)
+#define PROT1_MASK UINT32_C(0x40000)
+
+struct run {
+    const struct mt6762_conn_io *io;
+    struct mt6762_conn_report *r;
+    uint64_t stage_start, stage_budget;
+    uint32_t stage_iterations;
+};
+static int fail(struct run *s, int error)
+{
+    s->r->result=error;
+    return error;
+}
+static int deadline(struct run *s)
+{
+    uint64_t now=s->io->ticks(s->io->context);
+    s->r->ended_ticks=now;
+    if(now-s->r->began_ticks >= (uint64_t)s->io->total_timeout_us*13 ||
+       now-s->stage_start >= s->stage_budget)
+        return fail(s,MT6762_CONN_TIMEOUT);
+    return 0;
+}
+static void stage(struct run *s, enum mt6762_conn_stage value, uint32_t us)
+{
+    s->r->stage=value;
+    s->stage_start=s->io->ticks(s->io->context);
+    s->stage_budget=(uint64_t)us*13;
+    s->stage_iterations=0;
+}
+static int iteration(struct run *s)
+{
+    if(deadline(s))return s->r->result;
+    if(s->stage_iterations++ >= s->io->iteration_limit)
+        return fail(s,MT6762_CONN_ITERATION_LIMIT);
+    s->r->iterations++;
+    return 0;
+}
+static int admission(struct run *s)
+{
+    if(deadline(s))return s->r->result;
+    s->r->prerequisite_checks++;
+    int error=s->io->prerequisites(s->io->context,s->r->stage);
+    if(error) {
+        s->r->callback_error=error;
+        return fail(s,MT6762_CONN_PREREQUISITE);
+    }
+    return deadline(s);
+}
+static int read_word(struct run *s, uint32_t address, uint32_t *value)
+{
+    if(admission(s))return s->r->result;
+    s->r->last_address=address;
+    s->r->last_value_valid=0;s->r->last_access_write=0;
+    uint32_t raw=0;
+    int error=s->io->read32(s->io->context,address,&raw);
+    s->r->reads++;
+    if(error) {
+        s->r->callback_error=error;
+        return fail(s,MT6762_CONN_IO);
+    }
+    *value=raw;
+    s->r->last_value=raw;s->r->last_value_valid=1;
+    if(address==RGU)s->r->reset_observed=!!(raw&RESET);
+    if(address==CHIP_ID) {s->r->id=raw;s->r->id_valid=1;}
+    return deadline(s);
+}
+static int write_word(struct run *s, uint32_t address, uint32_t value)
+{
+    if(admission(s))return s->r->result;
+    s->r->last_address=address;s->r->last_value=value;
+    s->r->last_value_valid=1;s->r->last_access_write=1;
+    s->r->write_attempts++;
+    if(address==RGU)s->r->reset_write_attempted=1;
+    if(address==SPM)s->r->power_write_attempted=1;
+    s->io->barrier(s->io->context);
+    int error=s->io->write32(s->io->context,address,value);
+    s->io->barrier(s->io->context);
+    if(error) {
+        s->r->callback_error=error;
+        return fail(s,MT6762_CONN_IO);
+    }
+    s->r->writes++;
+    return deadline(s);
+}
+static int require_field(struct run *s, uint32_t address, uint32_t mask,
+    uint32_t expected, int mismatch)
+{
+    uint32_t value;
+    if(read_word(s,address,&value))return s->r->result;
+    if((value&mask)!=expected)return fail(s,mismatch);
+    return 0;
+}
+static int snapshot(struct run *s, int cold)
+{
+    static const uint32_t addr[8]={RGU,SPM,ACK0,ACK1,PROT_EN,PROT_ACK,PROT1_EN,PROT1_ACK};
+    static const uint32_t mask[8]={RESET,0x1f,2,2,PROT_MASK,PROT_MASK,PROT1_MASK,PROT1_MASK};
+    const uint32_t expected_cold[8]={0,0x12,0,0,PROT_MASK,PROT_MASK,PROT1_MASK,PROT1_MASK};
+    const uint32_t expected_ready[8]={RESET,0x0d,2,2,0,0,0,0};
+    for(unsigned i=0;i<8;i++) {
+        uint32_t value;
+        if(read_word(s,addr[i],&value))return s->r->result;
+        s->r->snapshot[i]=value;s->r->snapshot_valid|=1u<<i;
+        /* RGU can already be asserted while cold. Accept only a clear key
+         * readback or the exact shipped key, never invent another key. */
+        if(cold && i==0) {
+            uint32_t key=value&UINT32_C(0xff000000);
+            if(key && key!=RESET_KEY)return fail(s,MT6762_CONN_NOT_COLD);
+        } else if((value&mask[i])!=(cold?expected_cold[i]:expected_ready[i]))
+            return fail(s,cold?MT6762_CONN_NOT_COLD:MT6762_CONN_STATE_CHANGED);
+    }
+    return 0;
+}
+static int spm_transition(struct run *s, enum mt6762_conn_stage next,
+    uint32_t before, uint32_t after)
+{
+    stage(s,next,s->io->transition_timeout_us);
+    if(require_field(s,RGU,RESET,RESET,MT6762_CONN_STATE_CHANGED))return s->r->result;
+    if(next>=MT6762_CONN_ENABLE_CLOCK &&
+       (require_field(s,ACK0,2,2,MT6762_CONN_STATE_CHANGED) ||
+        require_field(s,ACK1,2,2,MT6762_CONN_STATE_CHANGED)))return s->r->result;
+    uint32_t value;
+    if(read_word(s,SPM,&value))return s->r->result;
+    if((value&0x1f)!=before)return fail(s,MT6762_CONN_STATE_CHANGED);
+    if(write_word(s,SPM,(value&~UINT32_C(0x1f))|after))return s->r->result;
+    return require_field(s,SPM,0x1f,after,MT6762_CONN_STATE_CHANGED);
+}
+static int wait_power(struct run *s)
+{
+    stage(s,MT6762_CONN_POWER_ACK,s->io->transition_timeout_us);
+    for(;;) {
+        uint32_t first,second;
+        if(iteration(s) || read_word(s,ACK0,&first) || read_word(s,ACK1,&second))return s->r->result;
+        if((first&2) && (second&2))return 0;
+        s->io->relax(s->io->context);
+    }
+}
+static int release_protection(struct run *s, enum mt6762_conn_stage next,
+    uint32_t address, uint32_t clear, uint32_t enable, uint32_t ack,
+    uint32_t mask, uint32_t before, uint32_t after)
+{
+    stage(s,next,s->io->transition_timeout_us);
+    if(require_field(s,RGU,RESET,RESET,MT6762_CONN_STATE_CHANGED) ||
+       require_field(s,SPM,0x1f,0x0d,MT6762_CONN_STATE_CHANGED) ||
+       require_field(s,ACK0,2,2,MT6762_CONN_STATE_CHANGED) ||
+       require_field(s,ACK1,2,2,MT6762_CONN_STATE_CHANGED) ||
+       require_field(s,enable,mask,before,MT6762_CONN_STATE_CHANGED) ||
+       require_field(s,ack,mask,before,MT6762_CONN_STATE_CHANGED) ||
+       write_word(s,address,clear))return s->r->result;
+    /* These bounded ordinary readbacks are stricter than stock's release
+     * function, which issues three CLR writes without waiting for ACK. */
+    for(;;) {
+        uint32_t en,sta;
+        if(iteration(s) || read_word(s,enable,&en) || read_word(s,ack,&sta))return s->r->result;
+        if((en&mask)==after && (sta&mask)==after)return 0;
+        s->io->relax(s->io->context);
+    }
+}
+static int wait_us(struct run *s, uint32_t us)
+{
+    uint64_t start=s->io->ticks(s->io->context);
+    for(;;) {
+        if(iteration(s))return s->r->result;
+        if(s->io->ticks(s->io->context)-start >= (uint64_t)us*13)return 0;
+        s->io->relax(s->io->context);
+    }
+}
+int mt6762_conn_power_reset_held(const struct mt6762_conn_io *io,
+    struct mt6762_conn_report *r, int enabled)
+{
+    if(!r)return MT6762_CONN_ARGUMENT;
+    /* Freestanding-friendly explicit initialization, no runtime memset. */
+    volatile unsigned char *bytes=(volatile unsigned char *)r;
+    for(unsigned i=0;i<sizeof(*r);i++)bytes[i]=0;
+    if(!enabled) {r->result=MT6762_CONN_DISABLED;return r->result;}
+    if(enabled!=1 || !io || !io->read32 || !io->write32 || !io->ticks ||
+       !io->barrier || !io->relax || !io->prerequisites || io->counter_hz!=13000000 ||
+       !io->transition_timeout_us || io->transition_timeout_us>100000 ||
+       !io->total_timeout_us || io->total_timeout_us>1000000 ||
+       !io->iteration_limit || io->iteration_limit>10000000) {
+        r->result=MT6762_CONN_ARGUMENT;return r->result;
+    }
+    struct run s={io,r,0,0,0};
+    r->began_ticks=io->ticks(io->context);
+    stage(&s,MT6762_CONN_COLD_ENTRY,io->transition_timeout_us);
+    /* Two masked cold observations before ANY writes. They are sequential,
+     * not atomic; the caller's exclusive ownership is essential. */
+    if(snapshot(&s,1) || snapshot(&s,1))return r->result;
+    stage(&s,MT6762_CONN_ASSERT_RESET,io->transition_timeout_us);
+    uint32_t reset;
+    if(read_word(&s,RGU,&reset) || write_word(&s,RGU,reset|RESET_KEY|RESET) ||
+       require_field(&s,RGU,RESET,RESET,MT6762_CONN_STATE_CHANGED))return r->result;
+    if(spm_transition(&s,MT6762_CONN_POWER_ON,0x12,0x16) ||
+       spm_transition(&s,MT6762_CONN_POWER_ON_SECONDARY,0x16,0x1e) ||
+       wait_power(&s) ||
+       spm_transition(&s,MT6762_CONN_ENABLE_CLOCK,0x1e,0x0e) ||
+       spm_transition(&s,MT6762_CONN_REMOVE_ISOLATION,0x0e,0x0c) ||
+       spm_transition(&s,MT6762_CONN_DOMAIN_RESET_B,0x0c,0x0d) ||
+       release_protection(&s,MT6762_CONN_RELEASE_PROTECT_14_16,PROT_CLR,0x14000,
+           PROT_EN,PROT_ACK,PROT_MASK,0x16000,0x2000) ||
+       release_protection(&s,MT6762_CONN_RELEASE_PROTECT_13,PROT_CLR,0x2000,
+           PROT_EN,PROT_ACK,PROT_MASK,0x2000,0) ||
+       release_protection(&s,MT6762_CONN_RELEASE_PROTECT1_18,PROT1_CLR,0x40000,
+           PROT1_EN,PROT1_ACK,PROT1_MASK,0x40000,0))return r->result;
+    stage(&s,MT6762_CONN_SETTLE,io->transition_timeout_us);
+    if(wait_us(&s,10))return r->result;
+    stage(&s,MT6762_CONN_READ_ID,200000);
+    /* Stock probes at 20 ms intervals. Isolate the ordinary ID load here;
+     * the rest of polling_consys_chipid performs patch/configuration writes. */
+    for(unsigned attempt=0;attempt<10;attempt++) {
+        uint32_t id;
+        if(iteration(&s) || snapshot(&s,0) || read_word(&s,CHIP_ID,&id))return r->result;
+        if(id==EXPECTED_ID) {
+            if(admission(&s))return r->result;
+            r->stage=MT6762_CONN_RESET_HELD_ID_VERIFIED;
+            r->result=MT6762_CONN_OK;return 0;
+        }
+        if(attempt!=9 && wait_us(&s,20000))return r->result;
+    }
+    return fail(&s,MT6762_CONN_ID_MISMATCH);
+}
diff --git a/tools/mt6762/hardware/connectivity-power/conn_power.h b/tools/mt6762/hardware/connectivity-power/conn_power.h
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..5d22827241e386c90b4442e4dc2250403bcdf915
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tools/mt6762/hardware/connectivity-power/conn_power.h
@@ -0,0 +1,64 @@
+/* SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
+ * Bounded MT6762 digital CONN cold start, ending with MCU reset held.
+ * No PMIC/clock setup, EMI programming, firmware patch, DMA or radio control.
+ */
+#ifndef MT6762_CONN_POWER_H
+#define MT6762_CONN_POWER_H
+#include <stdint.h>
+
+enum mt6762_conn_stage {
+    MT6762_CONN_NONE, MT6762_CONN_COLD_ENTRY, MT6762_CONN_ASSERT_RESET,
+    MT6762_CONN_POWER_ON, MT6762_CONN_POWER_ON_SECONDARY,
+    MT6762_CONN_POWER_ACK, MT6762_CONN_ENABLE_CLOCK,
+    MT6762_CONN_REMOVE_ISOLATION, MT6762_CONN_DOMAIN_RESET_B,
+    MT6762_CONN_RELEASE_PROTECT_14_16, MT6762_CONN_RELEASE_PROTECT_13,
+    MT6762_CONN_RELEASE_PROTECT1_18, MT6762_CONN_SETTLE,
+    MT6762_CONN_READ_ID, MT6762_CONN_RESET_HELD_ID_VERIFIED
+};
+enum mt6762_conn_result {
+    MT6762_CONN_OK=0, MT6762_CONN_DISABLED=1,
+    MT6762_CONN_ARGUMENT=-1, MT6762_CONN_PREREQUISITE=-2,
+    MT6762_CONN_IO=-3, MT6762_CONN_NOT_COLD=-4,
+    MT6762_CONN_STATE_CHANGED=-5, MT6762_CONN_TIMEOUT=-6,
+    MT6762_CONN_ITERATION_LIMIT=-7, MT6762_CONN_ID_MISMATCH=-8
+};
+struct mt6762_conn_io {
+    void *context;
+    int (*read32)(void *, uint32_t address, uint32_t *value);
+    int (*write32)(void *, uint32_t address, uint32_t value);
+    uint64_t (*ticks)(void *);
+    void (*barrier)(void *); /* actual device ordering, e.g. DSB SY */
+    void (*relax)(void *);   /* bounded, nonblocking, e.g. ARM YIELD */
+    /* Zero only while REAL independently established prerequisites remain
+     * valid under caller-held exclusive ownership. Called before each access.
+     * It is not an authentication/measurement mechanism or a permission grant.
+     * Caller owns PMIC, oscillator, A-die pinmux, EMI/remap+reserved memory,
+     * AP mapping/access, external-LDO policy and stable timer prerequisites.
+     */
+    int (*prerequisites)(void *, enum mt6762_conn_stage);
+    uint32_t counter_hz;            /* exactly 13000000 */
+    uint32_t transition_timeout_us; /* 1..100000; proposed default 100000 */
+    uint32_t total_timeout_us;      /* 1..1000000; proposed default 1000000 */
+    uint32_t iteration_limit;       /* 1..10000000 per stage; includes waits */
+};
+/* Diagnostic values are last successful observations, never a wire record or
+ * a claim that reset remains held after ownership/access is lost. There is no
+ * implicit retry/rollback. Failed writes may have reached hardware. */
+struct mt6762_conn_report {
+    enum mt6762_conn_stage stage;
+    int result, callback_error;
+    uint32_t last_address, last_value;
+    uint32_t last_value_valid, last_access_write;
+    uint32_t reads, write_attempts, writes, prerequisite_checks, iterations;
+    uint32_t reset_write_attempted, reset_observed, power_write_attempted;
+    uint32_t id_valid, id;
+    uint32_t snapshot[8], snapshot_valid; /* RGU, SPM, ACK0/1, EN0/ACK0, EN1/ACK1 */
+    uint64_t began_ticks, ended_ticks;
+};
+/* enabled=0 produces DISABLED without callbacks; exactly1 executes. The caller
+ * must hold ownership for the full call AND retain it on either success or
+ * failure until a separate recovery/lifetime owner takes over. This function
+ * never releases MCU reset and never powers anything off on error. */
+int mt6762_conn_power_reset_held(const struct mt6762_conn_io *,
+    struct mt6762_conn_report *, int enabled);
+#endif
